Z||000000||FieroLisa||01-19-2001||02:20 PM||||I did a search for this topic and it didn't come up with anything. I'm wondering the amount of money I should expect to pay to have Suspension Techniques lowering springs (which I already have) installed on my car. I had one place quote me at around $300 - and that was a place that had previously given me good deals. Is this normal?||||reg||6
Z||000001||Oreif||01-19-2001||02:31 PM||||Does the $300 include the alignment? If it does then yes it's a good price. When installing lowering springs, an alignment will be required. Usually the rears aren't bad. The fronts could be a pain depending on the condition of the bolts and such.||||reg||1
Z||000002||turbo86se||01-19-2001||02:33 PM||||My mechanic did mine for $100, this is the friend-rate, but I'm sure he wouldn't charge you that much more. He installed my ST springs on my 86SE. Bring it down here to Myrtle, we'll do it for ya!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=226077&a=1676320&p=20236791"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||KEV||01-19-2001||03:12 PM||||I was quoted $300-$500+$150 to do a aligment, so i did it my self, it was not do hard to do. to remove the fronts it took to people. It was a learning experinace.||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroLisa||01-19-2001||03:38 PM||||I just want it lowered by Daytona, but I won't have the GT in SC before then  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  I don't remember if the $300 incl. alignment, I'll have to call and ask again. I'd be afraid to do it myself, I'd end up killing myself trying to the front.<BR>But some exciting news, rogergarrison on the list has been a ton of help to me, letting me use his garage and good tools so I'll get started on my interior shortly! (and he has a fun 3.1 turbo to drive  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  )<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (Sold!)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/pffsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||bHooper||01-19-2001||03:46 PM||||Lisa,<P>Installing the springs isnt a very difficult job... i did it, myself!<P>Perhaps Roger can help you, or if you come through Greensboro b4 Daytona, Bob or I could help you.<P>To install the fronts, you need to seperate the ball joints and tie rod ends, so that you can remove the knuckle (Make sure you have a jack under the lower control arm, and a chain through the spring and upper control arm).  Once that is out of the way, lower the jack and press down on the control arm (you may need to use a pry bar), the spring will pop out (scaring the bejezus out of you) and you are now free to install the new spring.<P>For the rears, remove the strut (as described  in the Haynes book), then remove the spring and install the new one.  Reinstall is a reverse procedure.<P>Oh yeah, dont forget to losen the shocks from the control arm on the front, b4 droping the jack.<P>Hope that helps.  If you decide you want to do it yourself, and have dificulties, feel free to email or call me.<P>hoop||||reg||14
Z||000006||FieroLisa||01-19-2001||03:50 PM||||Ahh please help me!! I will be in North Carolina the week before Daytona- like from that Friday night till Wed then Thurs the 23rd I'm going south. Any chance you can give me a hand then?<BR>I'm just about broke, I love saving money  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I will also be in Greensboro the 26th but without the GT- driving the good old tracer again.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (Sold!)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/pffsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Bob Englert||01-19-2001||06:10 PM||||Lisa:<P>The good news is installing lowering springs is a lot easier than reinstalling the stock GT springs in the Fiero.  I am sure Hoop and/or I can help you get them installed.  Hoop has installed lowering springs on his 86 GT, I have rebuilt several front suspensions with the stock springs.  <P>I have not yet found a good alignment shop for the Fiero.  Hopefully, before you are down I will have someone to recommend.<P><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
